From daad4a3821cfc9cd9f539999af810fa0c34f655a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cerroverb <cerroverb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:29:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Alien vs. Predator: work out the player mode's variables as
 the game does

The Board page's hook (000D20, 0B3C6A) set the two variables the game reads
from the player mode with modes 0 and 2 the other way round. The game's own
003C5E (003D3C-003D5A) sets 1C5 for modes 1 and 2 (one coin chute for all)
and 1C6 for mode 2 (two players only); with both 0 it keeps a credit count
for each player (00160A). So a board as it left the factory (mode 2) played
as three players with a chute each in Pure, taking the third player's coin
and start, and "Three, a chute each" played as two. The names in avsp.h
follow what the variables mean.

Found comparing work RAM with MAME frame by frame: the two bytes were the
first difference after power-on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017uZUcLorPMd5nBmW5X4g75
